These message types are [internal messages](https://docs.ton.org/llms/foundations/messages/internal/content.md), so another contract must send them. This example uses a V4 wallet as the sender. Sign `internal_signed` with the V5 owner's key; `internal_extension` instead requires an installed extension. The V4 key authorizes only the outer message. `internal_signed` cannot change signature authentication.

